From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:55:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] rust: gpio: add consumer descriptors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a minimal owner of a requested GPIO descriptor: request by connection
id, read and set the logical value from sleepable context, and release on
drop.

The descriptor is deliberately not device-managed. A driver whose open
files outlive unbinding must be able to release its lines during unbind
rather than when the device's resources are torn down.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h |  1 +
 rust/kernel/gpio.rs             | 84 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 rust/kernel/lib.rs              |  2 +
 3 files changed, 87 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 rust/kernel/gpio.rs

